    </comp>
    <comp lib="11" loc="(21,184)" name="Text">
      <a name="halign" val="center"/>
      <a name="text">If the input is not connected, or has an error (E) or floating (X) value, then the output will be an error. This default
behavior can be summarized with the truth table above.</a>
      <a name="valign" val="base"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="11" loc="(211,696)" name="Text">
      <a name="halign" val="center"/>
      <a name="text" val="&quot;"/>
      <a name="valign" val="base"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="11" loc="(250,82)" name="Callout">
      <a name="dx" val="-31"/>
      <a name="dy" val="41"/>
      <a name="halign" val="center"/>
      <a name="style" val="margin: 4px;"/>
      <a name="text" val="ouput"/>
      <a name="valign" val="base"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="11" loc="(27,483)" name="Text">
      <a name="halign" val="center"/>
      <a name="text">Instead of the default behavior described above, a NOT gate can be configured in special high-impedance output modes:
* If the output behavior is set to "0/floating", it behaves in "open-collector" (a.k.a. "open-drain") inverter mode, 
where output is either 0 (when the input is 1) or floating (when the input is 0). 
* If the output behavior is set to "floating/1", the output is either floating (when the input is 1) or 0 (when the input is 1).
When combined with pull-up or pull-down resistors, these modes can be used to create a circuit similar to a "wired-AND"
or "wired-OR". See example circuits below.</a>
      <a name="valign" val="base"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="11" loc="(279,317)" name="Callout">
      <a name="dx" val="-62"/>
      <a name="dy" val="41"/>
      <a name="halign" val="center"/>
      <a name="style" val="margin: 4px;"/>
      <a name="text" val="4-bit NOT gate"/>
      <a name="valign" val="base"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="11" loc="(29,713)" name="Text">
      <a name="font" val="SansSerif bold 14"/>
      <a name="halign" val="center"/>
      <a name="text" val="NOT Gate Attributes"/>
      <a name="valign" val="base"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="11" loc="(297,568)" name="Text">
      <a name="font" val="SansSerif bold 12"/>
      <a name="halign" val="center"/>
      <a name="text" val="Output behavior as 0/floating"/>
      <a name="valign" val="base"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="11" loc="(30,871)" name="Text">
      <a name="font" val="SansSerif bold 14"/>
      <a name="halign" val="center"/>
      <a name="text" val="Example Circuits"/>
      <a name="valign" val="base"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="11" loc="(32,458)" name="Text">
      <a name="font" val="SansSerif bold 14"/>
      <a name="halign" val="center"/>
      <a name="text" val="High-impedance Output Modes"/>
      <a name="valign" val="base"/>
    </comp>
    <comp lib="11" loc="(32,733)" name="Text">
      <a name="halign" val="center"/>
      <a name="text">Facing - Used to rotate the gate. You can also rotate the gate using arrow keys (up/down/left/right).
Data Bits - The width, in bits, of the gate's input and output.
Gate Size - Used to select a wide or narrow symbol.
Output Value - Configures the output behavior. Mode "0/1" is the traditional behavior, with the NOT gate outputing
either 0 or 1, depending on the input. Mode "0/floating" is open-collector (aka open-drain) behavior, so the NOT gate
either outputs 0 or leaves the output floating. Mode "floating/1" makes the NOT gate leave the output floating or output a 1.
Label - A label to appear above the gate.
Label Font - Font for the label.
</a>
      <a name="valign" val="base"/>
    </comp>
